{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal would provide self-contained residential units within the curtilage of existing houses, that would not have regard to the character and appearance of the surrounding area, and safety of pedestrian and vehicular movements, and would be in conflict with other Local Plan policies. The proposal would be unacceptable in principle and would fail to comply with Local Plan policy SC1 (Housing Growth).",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposal, due to its size, scale, and unsuitable location, as well as its lack of quality design and features, would result in an alien, contrived, cramped, and unbalanced addition to the street scene. This would negatively impact the character and appearance of the adjacent dwelling, the surrounding corner properties, and the broader area, contrary to Local Plan policies CC1 (Context and Character), CC2 (Urban Design and Architecture), SC1 (Housing Growth), and SC4 (Scale and Intensity of New Housing Development). Additionally, it contradicts London Plan policies D4 (Delivering Good Design) and D6 (Housing Quality and Standards).",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposal would result in conditions prejudicial to the free flow and safety of pedestrian and vehicular movements due to the introduction of a new crossover in the vicinity of a street tree, the inappropriate size and location of the vehicular gated which would serve the proposed parking spot to the rear, insufficient pedestrian and vehicular access arrangements and visibility splays. Therefore, the proposal would be contrary to London Plan policy T6.1 and Local Plan policy EC2, as well as the Council's adopted Residential Crossover and Off-Street Parking Policy.",
    "Reason : 4 - The submitted energy statement fails to demonstrate that the development would maximise energy savings at each step of the energy hierarchy. It is, therefore, contrary to Local Plan Policies EQ1 (Energy and Carbon Reduction) and EQ2 (Sustainable design and construction) and London Plan Policies SI2 (Minimising Greenhouse Gas Emissions)."
  ],
